# End-of-line policy. The tools are hand-edited on Windows (CRLF) and by agents and CI
# (LF), and with no policy git kept renormalizing docs/*.html and embeds/*.html, which
# showed as phantom "modified" files and made every merge fight the line endings rather
# than the change. These are the files that carry the real work and must byte-match
# between docs/ and embeds/, so they are pinned to LF and told not to be normalized on
# the way in or out. Everything else keeps git's default auto handling.

# The source and embed HTML the site serves: fixed to LF, no CRLF churn.
docs/*.html    text eol=lf
embeds/*.html  text eol=lf

# The Velo files pasted into Wix: same treatment so they don't churn either.
velo/**/*.js   text eol=lf

# Data and config that CI and agents read: LF so a Windows checkout doesn't rewrite them.
*.json         text eol=lf
scripts/*.js   text eol=lf

# Binary assets git should never touch.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
